  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Sebelipase alfa, a recombinant form of the enzyme lysosomal acid lipase, is used to treat lysosomal acid lipase deficiency, an inborn error of lipid metabolism. It is an approved enzyme medication authorised in the European Union.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q21789862&quot;>Wikidata Q21789862</a> and the WHO ATC classification and the EMA medicines list; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>sebelipase alfa</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>A16AB14</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB11563&quot;>DB11563</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q21789862&quot;>Q21789862</a></td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>55000 g/mol (Drugs.Common (25.09))</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
